# The identity and permission calls and their refusals, made through musl,
# which chooses the system calls itself.
musl/authmusl
musl/permmusl
musl/suidmusl
# After those three, since it rewrites files they read and puts them back. It
# is the slowest probe here: it waits out the credential lock's retry limit
# twice and sleeps once inside a held transaction.
musl/pwauthmusl
# After it, for the same reason: it runs the image's setuid passwd, which
# takes the same lock and rewrites the same files, and it restores all three
# databases before it exits.
musl/passwdmusl
musl/addusermusl
musl/loginmusl
rebootprobe
musl/readvmusl
musl/clockmusl
musl/statmusl
musl/stampmusl
musl/execargmusl
musl/spawnmusl
musl/sigmusl
